  <prompt>
    Add `Message = 100000004` to the C# `CommunicationType` enum so the code contract matches the EXISTING Dataverse `sprk_communicationtype` choice (FR-16, design §14.6). The enum currently has `Email=100000000`, `TeamsMessage=100000001`, `SMS=100000002`, `Notification=100000003` and is MISSING `Message`. This single value is load-bearing: `CommunicationChannelDispatcher` keys on `CommunicationType`, so the messaging sender/archiver (task 020) can only be dispatched once `Message` exists as an enum member.

    File: `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Models/CommunicationType.cs`.

    Confirm the integer against task 001's schema-audit (it verified the Dataverse `Message` choice = `100000004`). If 001 flagged a mismatch, STOP and escalate — do NOT hardcode a value that disagrees with Dataverse (the whole point of FR-16 is enum = Dataverse). Because this is a BFF-touching change (root §10), it carries the FULL BFF-hygiene protocol: build, publish-size delta vs the ~45.30 MB baseline, CVE scan, Step 9.5 quality gates, and `/conflict-check` before the PR — even though the change is one line, the protocol is unconditional for BFF edits.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer for the Communication subsystem. Authoritative on `Services/Communication/Models/` + the `CommunicationChannelDispatcher` keyed-dispatch pattern. Disciplined on root §10 BFF hygiene (publish-size, CVE, placement, conflict-check) even for small edits.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `CommunicationType.Message = 100000004` exists in the enum, matching the confirmed Dataverse choice. The BFF builds clean; the channel dispatcher can key on `Message`; publish-size delta (≈0 expected) + CVE result reported; Step 9.5 gates pass; `/conflict-check` run before the PR. Task 020 (messaging sender/archiver) can register + dispatch by `Message`.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §14.6 resolved: reuse the EXISTING `Message` Dataverse choice (not `TeamsMessage`), and extend the C# enum to match. FR-16 acceptance is literally "enum + Dataverse option-set agree on 100000004." Task 001 verifies the Dataverse side; this task fixes the code side.

      §11 note: this MODIFIES an existing file (adds one enum member) — no new component, so the §11 three-question template does not apply. The value's justification is the FR-16 contract (enum must match Dataverse for the dispatcher to resolve the messaging channel).

      Placement Justification (root §10): the enum lives in the existing BFF `Services/Communication/Models/` — it is a communication-domain contract already owned by the BFF; no new service, package, or DI registration is introduced. Cite `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`; the placement answer is "in BFF, in the existing model file — no new surface."
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Models/CommunicationType.cs (the enum to extend)</file>
