  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec FR-16">The enum value MUST be exactly `100000004` and MUST match the Dataverse `sprk_communicationtype` `Message` choice. If task 001 flagged a mismatch, STOP + escalate (root §6) — do not silently hardcode.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Change is additive: add the `Message` member only. Do NOT renumber/reorder the existing members (Email/TeamsMessage/SMS/Notification) — they are a persisted contract.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root §10">FULL BFF hygiene: `dotnet build` + publish-size delta vs ~45.30 MB (expect ≈0 for an enum add) + `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` (no new HIGH CVE) + Placement Justification citing `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` + `/conflict-check` before PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root §10 bullet 6">If any code consumes `CommunicationType` in a way that must handle the new value (e.g., an exhaustive switch without a default), update the corresponding tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/`. Grep for switch/dispatch sites on `CommunicationType`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032">The dispatcher stays unconditional; adding `Message` to the enum does NOT itself register a channel (that is task 020) — do not add conditional registration here.</constraint>
  </constraints>

